<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov beef imports off 28.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov beef imports off 28.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in November fell 28.7 percent to 42,535 tonnes from 59,652 tonnes in the same period a year earlier, according to data released by the Finance Ministry on Thursday. Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Nov 96	 Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p> Total	    42,535	 45,078     59,652</p>
<p> Refrigerated   25,011	 27,257     33,611</p>
<p> Frozen	   17,524	 17,821     26,041</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     14,461	 16,068     19,674</p>
<p>  U.S.	     9,945	 10,598     13,241</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Nov 96	 Oct 96    Oct 95</p>
<p> U.S.	     10,854	 11,075	14,793</p>
<p> Australia	 5,397	  5,062	 9,971</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first 11 months of 1996 were 292,851 tonnes against 330,616 tonnes during the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the first 11 months of 1996 were 288,859 tonnes against 260,959 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
